 You can find out more about all these settings in the [Rails Action Mailer documentation](https://guides.rubyonrails.org/action_mailer_basics.html#action-mailer-configuration).
 
+
+#### Web push
+
+To deliver tray notifications to phones and desktops, set a VAPID key pair:
+
+- `VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY`
+- `VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY`
+- `VAPID_SUBJECT` (optional, defaults to a `mailto:` address taken from `MAILER_FROM_ADDRESS`)
+
+Generate a key pair with `bin/rails runner 'key = WebPush.generate_key; puts key.public_key; puts key.private_key'`.
+If the keys are unset, the app still runs; people just won't be able to turn push on.
+
 #### Base URL
 
 Fizzy needs to know the public URL of your instance so it can generate correct links in certain situations (like when sending emails).
